TY  - JOUR
T1  - Randomized manipulation of early cognitive experience impacts adult brain structure
AN  - 2770725377; 2023-34503-014
AB  - Does early exposure to cognitive and linguistic stimulation impact brain structure? Or do genetic predispositions account for the co-occurrence of certain neuroanatomical phenotypes and a tendency to engage children in cognitively stimulating activities? Low socioeconomic status infants were randomized to either 5 years of cognitively and linguistically stimulating center-based care or a comparison condition. The intervention resulted in large and statistically significant changes in brain structure measured in midlife, particularly for male individuals. These findings are the first to extend the large literature on cognitive enrichment effects on animal brains to humans, and to demonstrate the effects of uniquely human features such as linguistic stimulation. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
 (Source: journal abstract)
