T1  - Nutrition and brain development: Social policy implications
AN  - 1011224876; 2002-06193-002
AB  - Notes that undernutrition among young children is widespread in the US and has a detrimental impact on brain development. The article explores the risks associated with undernutrition and the potential for recovery when diet and the environment improve. Three policy implications are discussed: (1) increasing access to federal food programs, (2) promoting breastfeeding, and (3) working toward reducing child poverty. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2025 APA, all rights reserved)
